==English==

===Pronunciation===
*{{audio|en-us-alimony.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Etymology===
Known since 1655, from {{etyl|la}} [[alimonia]] "food, support, nourishment, sustenance", itself from [[alere]] "to nourish" + [[-monia]] (signifying action, state, condition).

===Noun===
{{wikipedia}}
{{en-noun|alimonies}}

# {{legal}} A [[court]]-[[enforce]]d [[allowance]] made to a former [[spouse]] by a [[divorce]]d or [[legally]] [[separated]] person.
# The [[means]] to [[support]] [[life]].

